# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=shaman:elemental style=melee size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=390x844,touch save=carried (behaves as fresh, #273 --
# carried never actually carries across separate playbot invocations because
# the dev-server port is derived from the process pid).
#
# A fresh/carried save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26
# driver-lesson recipe), rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight
# "visiting" framing.
#
# What no session has done before: the one prior melee-style 25-heroic
# evening (rogue:assassination, 2026-09-27-7) crossed THE VIGIL clean in
# 24.5s, but direction.md read that off rogue's own flat moveSpeed=178, the
# highest in the roster (src/sim/classes.ts) -- an outlier this line already
# flagged as *not* further evidence for "size/difficulty, not style" separating
# a clean crossing from a #6 stall, since a faster class would cross clean
# anywhere by the same mechanism. shaman's own moveSpeed is 167, the same
# middle tier as druid/mage -- this is the first melee-style evening on a
# class whose speed is not the outlier, and so the first real second data
# point for whether `melee`'s own fixed beeline-at-target steering crosses
# corridors cleanly on its own merits at 25-heroic, or whether rogue's clean
# record was rogue, not melee.
#
# Second question the same cell opens: shaman:elemental is a ranged caster
# spec. direction.md's #7 already found a ranged spec forced into `melee`
# style (marksmanship hunter, then elemental shaman itself) dealing zero
# damage in a battleground, beelining into melee range and never landing a
# cast. That has never been measured inside an actual raid/evening at
# heroic -- whether a caster with no ranged attack still clears Bonegrinder
# heroic for free (line 1's shape) or whether standing in melee range against
# bonestorm (#267, already measured as reversing melee's own hit ratio) costs
# a caster body more than it costs an intended melee class.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:shaman:elemental
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening melee 200 5
state
shot end
says
bill
